second and Finke third. Paltrinieri could not maintain the pace, as Wiffen finished strongly to win the gold medal. Finke put on his patented fast finish, recording 26.47 and 55.30 for the final 50 and 100, but he could not catch Wiffen, who finished in 26.94 and 55.33."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Wiffen finished in 7:38.19, winning by 0.56 seconds, in an Olympic record by over three seconds and with the sixth fastest performance of all-time. Paltrinieri held on for the bronze medal, his fourth Olympic medal. Finke and Paltrinieri would return in five days and also go 1-2 in the 1,500, in that order. Wiffen’s medal made him only the third Irish swimmer, and the first man, to win an Olympic medal, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/48302"} "Michelle Smith"] " in 1996, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2505293"} "Mona McSharry"] " only the day before, in the women’s 100 metre breaststroke."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143924"} "Daniel Wiffen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRL.png"}] "IRL"]] [:td {} "7:41.53 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "7:38.19 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147477"} "Bobby Finke"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "7:43.00 (3 h3)"] [:td {} "7:38.75 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/124275"} "Gregorio Paltrinieri"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-r